2. $ (10, 10) $: $ 10 \cdot 10 = 100 $
3. $ (11, 11) $: $ 11 \cdot 11 = 121 $
4. $ (11, 9) $: $ 11 \cdot 9 = 99 $

We get **different** values of $ xy $: 100, 99, 120, 121 — so $ xy $ is **not constant**?

